From 78a62dce6dd62c389a2afab82cb26ee316c5e0d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:35:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat(plugin-sdk): validate plugin permissions against one
 vocabulary

Manifests request dotted permissions such as network.egress and
resource.write, while IsolationGuard compared free-form names like
"database", "network" and "admin". The two vocabularies never met: a
manifest requesting network.egress passed the restricted-rpc check, an
UNTRUSTED plugin could request platform.admin, and a manifest could list
any string at all.

Add forgemesh.plugin.permissions.Permission as the single vocabulary.
PluginSpec.permissions is now list[Permission] and rejects unknown and
duplicate names. The plugin-manifest JSON Schema enumerates the same
values (a contract test keeps the enum equal to the Python vocabulary),
so scripts/validate_manifests.py enforces it through the schema.
IsolationGuard.check_access and validate_manifest take vocabulary names
and raise IsolationError for names outside it instead of letting them
through as harmless.

Breaking: manifests and callers that use free-form names (metrics:read,
database, admin, ...) must switch to the dotted names. All ten shipped
manifests already use vocabulary names.
